ent of bitcoin's life has been at a  lower price if you bought bitcoin then  you held till today you are in profit if  we then go ahead and we take a look at  what i think is one of the most  important numbers in all of bitcoin that  compound annual growth rate you can see  that bitcoin continues over the last  decade to compound growth at 143  every year that is an incredible  performance the sharpe ratio of the five  years is still 1.5 or so which puts it  steadily above gold  s p 500 nasdaq or tlt if we then go  ahead and we take a look into will  clemente and block ware's newsletter  this week we've got two on-chain metrics  that we can show you the first is this  percent futures open interest but using  crypto as margin rather than stable  coins or anything else and you can see  that at the beginning of march we  started to see an uptick in that futures  open interest so it's something to  continue to pay attention to as more  leverage enters the system then if we go  and we look at whales what the hell are  the whales doing in bitcoin well we can  see that whales actually in the  beginning of march or kind of end of  february started to sell some of their  coins and what this really tells us is  that bitcoin is becoming more  distributed the whales hold less of it  but also it tells us that that's  probably where a lot of the cell  pressure is coming from even though we  have that geopolitical conflict even  though we have all the macro factors  bitcoin still is trading within this  like 35 to 45 000 range a lot of it's  probably because these whales are  actually have so much cell pressure in  the market and then lastly if we go  ahead and we take a look dylan leclair  had this great tweet that showed that  literally 30 000 bitcoin were taken off  a coin base just yesterday and so  ultimately what we're watching is that  there's a lot of action that's happening  in the bitcoin market but because  bitcoin is an open decentralized  protocol that the blockchain 